depgraph: remember per package and USE whether REQUIRED_USE is satisfied

Sub-series: I (REQUIRED_USE memo) - patch 1 of 1; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: unchanged (line numbers only)

_add_pkg() remembers per (package, enabled USE) whether REQUIRED_USE is
satisfied, for all backtracking attempts: the memo is kept in
_frozen_config, which the attempts share. Only the truth value is kept,
and an exception is not recorded.

This was one of the pieces of patch 0025 of the 25-patch ladder
(config-trims-and-leftovers), which is now patches 0022, 0025, 0026, 0027
and 0030. It stands before flatten-atoms-memo (0026) and
probe-certain-atoms (now 0029, formerly 0022) because the three add their
lines at the same place of _frozen_depgraph_config.__init__, and in this
order each of them applies without the others. The pieces of 0025 were not measured one by one
in the ladder; together, on top of patches 0001-0024: sum of six states
95.9 -> 90.5 s (-5.5 s, -1.2 % of the stock sum 447.5). Alone on stock
3.0.83: see README (sub-series I).

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21; cut out of its
former patch on 2026-11-21 without changing a line of code. Not a
human-written change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on
six states of one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the
same merge list in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts
and the same package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
---
--- a/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
+++ b/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
@@ -431,1 +431,3 @@
-        self._highest_license_masked = {}
+        # (pkg, enabled USE flags) -> bool, see depgraph._add_pkg.
+        self._required_use_sat_memo = {}
+        self._highest_license_masked = {}
@@ -4268,12 +4270,24 @@
             and pkg._metadata.get("REQUIRED_USE")
             and eapi_has_required_use(pkg.eapi)
         ):
-            required_use_is_sat = check_required_use(
-                pkg._metadata["REQUIRED_USE"],
-                self._pkg_use_enabled(pkg),
-                pkg.iuse.is_valid_flag,
-                eapi=pkg.eapi,
-            )
+            # Whether REQUIRED_USE is satisfied depends on the package (its
+            # metadata does not change) and on the enabled USE flags, and
+            # only the truth value is used here. Every backtracking run adds
+            # the same packages again, so the answer is kept for all of them
+            # in _frozen_config. Exceptions are not recorded.
+            pkg_use_enabled = self._pkg_use_enabled(pkg)
+            required_use_memo = self._frozen_config._required_use_sat_memo
+            required_use_is_sat = required_use_memo.get((pkg, pkg_use_enabled))
+            if required_use_is_sat is None:
+                required_use_is_sat = bool(
+                    check_required_use(
+                        pkg._metadata["REQUIRED_USE"],
+                        pkg_use_enabled,
+                        pkg.iuse.is_valid_flag,
+                        eapi=pkg.eapi,
+                    )
+                )
+                required_use_memo[(pkg, pkg_use_enabled)] = required_use_is_sat
             if not required_use_is_sat:
                 if dep.atom is not None and dep.parent is not None:
                     self._add_parent_atom(pkg, (dep.parent, dep.atom))
